| **Total** | **14,939** | **35** | |

Weeks start on Monday at local midnight. The final row covers October 26–31, through the snapshot’s last retained source message at **October 31, 10:45:02 PDT**. The largest recorded activity falls in the midterm week of October 5 and the follow-up and selection week of October 12. The [timeline](timeline.md) explains those programs and the earlier phases.

The earliest retained message is **September 7, 13:08:33 PDT**, asking about the philosophy competition; its [original timestamp and text](../logs/codex/chats/01a07d7c-05c5-7091-a7cc-692e19ff8fca/conversation.md#source-line-9) are preserved. The later GitHub import date is not used to date the work.

## What these counts mean

Each message object in the [morning snapshot index](../logs/updates/20261031-final-verification/baseline-index.json) is counted once, using its original source time: 14,871 carry `source_timestamp`, and 68 archive-view records retain it as `timestamp`. All 14,939 have a valid, timezone-qualified source time. Unknown, invalid, unzoned, or explicitly synthetic timestamps are excluded; there are **zero such exclusions in this frozen export**. Capture times, file dates, and Git commit dates do not enter the counts. Original conversation files and bundle members are identified by hashes in the index and [morning snapshot bundle manifest](../logs/updates/20261031-final-verification/baseline-bundles-manifest.json).

The preserved [activity calculation](../evidence/repository-audit/20261031/history/activity.json) still names `logs/index.json` as its historical input. For that reference, use the morning snapshot index linked above: its bytes and SHA-256 are unchanged. The current index describes a later union.

These are message counts, not counts of human contributions, finished reviews, essays, or hours worked. Agent task prompts can carry the `user` role. A week with fewer messages does not establish inactivity: per-session cutoffs and missing or excluded records limit coverage. Accepted Claude fragments, tool records, and [later receipts](../logs/updates/20261031-late-receipts/MANIFEST.json) are separate, sometimes overlapping evidence and are not added to this Codex message total.

The denominator is the preserved 13,880-message export plus 1,059 recovered visible messages. The [union plan](../logs/updates/20261031-complete-visible/union-plan.json), [recovery summary](../logs/updates/20261031-complete-visible/native-recovery-summary.json), [source cutoffs](../logs/updates/20261031-complete-visible/native-source-cutoffs.json), and [frozen export manifest](../logs/updates/20261031-complete-visible/MANIFEST.json) describe that recovery and its remaining gaps. The later [final supplement](../logs/updates/20261031-final-verification/MANIFEST.json) brings the current union to 15,302 messages, including eight labelled inherited copies. Those additions do not change this frozen activity table.
